# The built executable, named for the package.
/slate

# What `bench/pgo.sh` builds and trains with: the instrumented binary, its counter files, the merged
# profile and the profile-guided binary. All of it is one machine's measurement and none of it is source.
/pgo/

# IntelliJ.
.idea/

# What `tests/js/p8.sl` writes and takes away again. It is here for the run that does not get to the
# end, since a differential test that left its own leavings behind would not say the same thing twice.
/tests/js/scratch/

# The root `tests/js/p29.sl` serves and the file above it that a traversal would reach, for the same
# reason: both are made and taken away by the program.
/tests/js/pubroot/
/tests/js/pubsecret.txt

# Anything `slate js` wrote. The corpus harness in `tests_js_run.sysl` writes `<program>.js` beside
# each program and removes it when the two back ends agree, so what is left is the evidence of a
# failure; `examples/web/` and `tests/js/dom/` are built when somebody wants to open the page.
#
# **Generated output is not checked in, deliberately.** A committed `counter.js` would open without a
# build step and be wrong the first time anybody changed the framework under it, silently — the
# README beside it names the one command instead.
*.sl.js
*.slx.js
/examples/web/counter.js
/tests/js/dom/counter.js

# A probe's own run-unique temp file, made and removed by `probe_path`/`probe_name` in
# `tests_kit_cli.sysl` -- named so two suites racing on this tree never share a fixed path.
# `*.sl.js` above already covers its compiled `.js`; this covers the source and a stray `.mjs`.
/tests/*.tmp.sl
/tests/*.tmp.sl.mjs
/tests/*-driver.tmp.js
/tests/mods/*.tmp.sl
